WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:09.080
I only have one experience

2
00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:13.720
where I was made to feel guilty
about leaving Estonia.

3
00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:16.920
A friend of mine
who I'm still friends with,

4
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.440
but a bit differently, because
I can't forget that sentence.

5
00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:34.000
GENERATION BEYOND BORDERS

6
00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:38.400
AMBASSADORS

7
00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:43.400
I don't even remember the situation,
but she was somehow unhappy.

8
00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:46.360
She had problems with money
and work and everything.

9
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.600
I asked, why don't you consider
going somewhere else

10
00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:52.960
where you might be happier?

11
00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:56.840
Then I got an avalanche of information,

12
00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:01.400
that because of people like you who
are leaving and not supporting Estonia,

13
00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:07.040
people like me have to suffer here
to preserve Estonian culture and life.

14
00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:17.320
Sometimes it makes me feel a bit bad

15
00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:21.320
or I don't feel like dealing with it
and justifying and explaining it,

16
00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:25.480
is a question of where I live
or why I have such an accent.

17
00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:28.120
It's tiring sometimes.

18
00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:32.120
As if it wasn't enough that I still
speak Estonian and speak it well,

19
00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:35.360
does my accent have to put me
in a category for you?

20
00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:39.560
Do you need this compartmentalization
and what does it give you?

21
00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:43.360
What does it really tell you
about me as a person?

22
00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:46.320
Am I more or less Estonian?

23
00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:50.000
And if I explain that
I've been away for 10 or 12 years,

24
00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:53.960
is that good or bad,
does that legitimize my accent?

25
00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:58.120
Or is 12 years such a long time
that you're no longer Estonian?

26
00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:06.000
I remember when they talked
about comfort refugees,

27
00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:11.600
it seemed really funny,
because for the first ten years,

28
00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:14.960
when I was in the midst of emigration,
I wasn't comfortable.

29
00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:17.720
I don't know how being
an immigrant is comfortable.

30
00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:21.160
It's interesting,
you have some challenges,

31
00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:25.760
you learn a lot,
but it's far from comfortable.

32
00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:28.680
Maybe I am comfortable
in California because it's warm,

33
00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:30.720
but I don't even like
the heat that much,

34
00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:32.880
in fact, I'm uncomfortable there,
too hot.

35
00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:40.320
I've felt guilty or bad,
for example, with our families.

36
00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:42.680
Why did we do this to them?
- Yeah.

37
00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:44.320
But other people?

38
00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:48.400
Even with my friends,
some of my friends, I still felt that

39
00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:55.840
I was a traitor or something...
There was that.

40
00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:00.200
When we came back the second time...
- To England.

41
00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:01.880
How little good luck was wished to us?

42
00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:10.960
I think when the phrase
"comfort refugee" was coined,

43
00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:14.680
the idea was to make people
who have gone abroad

44
00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:16.480
feel uncomfortable.

45
00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:21.000
We haven't been to Estonia,
I don't know if it's used,

46
00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:23.040
if it's talked about,
I don't feel...

47
00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:26.280
No, I think it depends
on the circle you're in.

48
00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:31.440
I'm sure there are people
who still consider us like...

49
00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:34.680
Traitors?
- Traitors, yes. Definitely.

50
00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:45.680
I feel that people in Estonia think

51
00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:49.080
that those who go abroad to work

52
00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:51.040
betray their homeland,

53
00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:55.280
they don't contribute
and just look for a better life.

54
00:03:56.280 --> 00:04:01.440
But I'm here in Norway,
and I'm contributing.

55
00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:07.560
Thanks to this,
we have 40 jobs in Estonia that

56
00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:11.240
directly benefit from me being here

57
00:04:11.320 --> 00:04:14.800
and making contacts on the spot.

58
00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:20.040
When I graduated from university,
I felt a little guilty

59
00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:23.160
that the state was educating me

60
00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:29.080
and that my goal was to go abroad.

61
00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:35.000
Ten years later,
I've kind of made peace with it.

62
00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:39.280
We've built a company that

63
00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:47.000
creates value for Estonia,

64
00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:54.120
and I feel like this issue
is over for me.

65
00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:59.080
It was rather good that the
Estonian state gave me an education,

66
00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:01.240
now it's getting it back
many times over.

67
00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:11.360
Many Estonians living abroad
still have very strong ties to Estonia.

68
00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:18.040
Estonians living abroad
must be taken into account.

69
00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:24.760
They should not be condemned
or criticized,

70
00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:33.240
but rather they should be considered
as part of Estonian society,

71
00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:39.520
because there is a good chance that
many of them would return to Estonia

72
00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:45.840
if they were less condemned,

73
00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:49.560
if they were more expected.

74
00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:58.880
Every Estonian living abroad
actually contributes to Estonia

75
00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:02.560
by introducing Estonia to the world.

76
00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:17.000
When I went to Edinburgh,

77
00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:24.200
then looking from there,
Estonia seemed more and more...

78
00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:27.600
close to my heart and very dear.

79
00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:30.120
Hence the connection with Estonia,

80
00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:34.600
I wanted to somehow contribute to the
development and society of Estonia.

81
00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:41.960
Being abroad, representing the
Estonian state just by your presence,

82
00:06:42.440 --> 00:06:45.720
if more people in the world
know about Estonia,

83
00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:50.480
have a personal relationship
with Estonia, through some friends,

84
00:06:50.600 --> 00:06:56.080
then in fact it also strengthens
Estonia's security.

85
00:06:56.160 --> 00:06:58.120
If something happens,

86
00:06:58.200 --> 00:07:02.800
there are more people in the world
who care about Estonia.

87
00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:08.520
I believe this is something
each of us can do.

88
00:07:14.440 --> 00:07:16.960
These roots, these Estonian roots.

89
00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:20.760
I feel like ever since Erasmus,
I've been pushing these

90
00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:23.440
Estonian stories on all foreigners,

91
00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:29.640
as if I had some obligation
to tell the world that

92
00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:35.480
there is this little Estonia somewhere
and nobody really cares.

93
00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:40.080
The further you go from Estonia,

94
00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:45.920
the more you become interested
in everything related to Estonia.

95
00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:51.600
Suddenly there's a huge urge
to buy Saaremaa patterned tablecloths,

96
00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:59.520
Haapsalu shawls, wooden butter knives,
which I didn't have in Estonia.

97
00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:08.520
I think I've become more Estonian
even when I'm away from Estonia.

98
00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:13.240
I have to work harder to preserve
Estonian culture and things.

99
00:08:13.360 --> 00:08:15.320
On the anniversary
of the Republic of Estonia,

100
00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:19.160
when I was in Estonia,
I didn't do much.

101
00:08:19.240 --> 00:08:23.640
In America, I throw an awesome party
every year for a hundred people.

102
00:08:23.720 --> 00:08:29.040
I bake Estonian bread,
I make pork roast, sauerkraut.

103
00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:30.920
Everything, spray on bread!

104
00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:34.280
People come,
they hear stories about Estonia,

105
00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:36.800
they taste all these things.

106
00:08:36.880 --> 00:08:41.200
I'm like the Estonian ambassador
in America, well a "little ambassador."

107
00:08:41.280 --> 00:08:46.200
It's been my very frequent experience
that for most Americans,

108
00:08:46.320 --> 00:08:49.560
I'm the first Estonian
they've ever met.

109
00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:52.400
I'm the stereotype
of Estonians to them.

110
00:08:52.440 --> 00:08:54.960
From now on,
they think Estonians are like that.

111
00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:57.480
It's a pretty big responsibility.

112
00:08:57.560 --> 00:09:02.360
I have to hold the Estonian flag high
by being a nice and good person.

113
00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:11.120
The greatest value
of leaving home is that

114
00:09:11.240 --> 00:09:13.720
you understand who you are.

115
00:09:13.800 --> 00:09:18.560
Another thing is that you understand
how life works on planet Earth.

116
00:09:18.720 --> 00:09:21.120
What is, for example, in Estonian life,

117
00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:24.600
what is an Estonian thing
and what is universal.

118
00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:29.760
Friendship, love etc.
are like that everywhere.

119
00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:31.560
And the love of nature,

120
00:09:31.640 --> 00:09:34.200
although nature is different,
people still love nature.

121
00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:38.440
There are many
universal themes of humanity.

122
00:09:38.520 --> 00:09:41.120
There is also a lot of unique Estonia.

123
00:09:41.240 --> 00:09:43.000
Until you leave Estonia,

124
00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:45.720
you won't know
what makes Estonia unique.

125
00:09:46.040 --> 00:09:47.640
GENERATION BEYOND BORDERS
